 prevalence of <italic>Ancylostoma </italic>species infection in dogs associated with endemic focus of human cutaneous larva migrans in Tacuaremba Uruguay</article-title><source>Parasite</source><year>1996</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>131</fpage><lpage>134</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8758550</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patz</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Gractzyk</surname><given-names>TK</given-names></name><name><surname>Gella</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Vittor</surname><given-names>AY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of environmental changes on emerging parasitic diseases</article-title><source>Int J Parasitol</source><year>2002</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1395</fpage><lpage>1405</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11113264</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0020-7519(00)00141-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dada</surname><given-names>BJO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Taeniasis, cysticercosis and echinococcosis/hydatidiosis in Nigeria: iv. Prevalence of <italic>Echinococcus granulosus </italic>infection in stray dogs</article-title><source>J Helminthol</source><year>1980</year><volume>54</volume><fpage>299</fpage><lpage>301</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7229324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ayanwale</surname><given-names>FO</given-names></name><name><surname>Dipeolu</surname><given-names>OO</given-names></name><name><surname>Esuruoso</surname><given-names>GO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The incidence of <italic>Echinococcus </italic>infection in dogs, sheep and goats slaughtered in Ibadan, Nigeria</article-title><source>Int J Zoonoses</source><year>1982</year><volume>9</volume><fpage>65</fpage><lpage>68</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7174236</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiejina</surname><given-names>SN</given-names></name><name><surname>Ekwe</surname><given-names>TO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Canine toxocariasis and the associated environmental contamination of urban areas in Eastern Nigeria</article-title><source>Vet Parasitol</source><year>1986</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>161</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3788022</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0304-4017(86)90019-1</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Anene</surname><given-names>BM</given-names></name><name><surname>Nnaji</surname><given-names>TO</given-names></name><name><surname>Chime</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intestinal Parasitic infections of dogs in the Nsukka area of Enugu, Nigeria</article-title><source>Prev Vet Med</source><year>1996</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>89</fpage><lpage>94</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0167-5877(95)00527-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Forrester</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Scott</surname><given-names>ME</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Measurement of <italic>Ascaris </italic>infection intensity and dynamic of expulsion following treatment with Mebendazole</article-title><source>Parasitology</source><year>1990</year><volume>100</volume><fpage>303</fpage><lpage>308</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2345663</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pitchford</su